MID_SE_Ism_Seo_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Ism_Seo_A_001: I have seen the plans. Convey my gratitude to their\ndraftsman. You are dismissed.
MID_SE_Ism_Seo_A_002: Yet another thorny problem. Restoring the holy land\nwill not go so easily as I had hoped.
MID_SE_Ism_Seo_A_003: <NCA>"You seem busy."
MID_SE_Ism_Seo_A_004: <NCB>"Is this about Cybele?"
MID_SE_Ism_Seo_A_005: <ACA>Indeed. There are many preparations to make before\nmy kingdom can annex the county of Cybele.
MID_SE_Ism_Seo_A_006: <ACB>Yes. Even during wartime, a queen must look ahead\nto what lies beyond for her people.
MID_SE_Ism_Seo_A_007: There's the work rebuilding the temple of Yu Phas,\nas well as the Lake Brontes canal project.
MID_SE_Ism_Seo_A_008: And I must found a school for literacy, as I promised\nBonaventure.
MID_SE_Ism_Seo_A_009: The largest problem is the temple. I had planned it\naround Aurora, the sole daughter of Yu Phas.
MID_SE_Ism_Seo_A_010: But she prefers a more human life, and I must\nrespect those wishes.
MID_SE_Ism_Seo_A_011: I considered Yu Phas herself, but I will not bind her\nonce more to the needs of humanity.
MID_SE_Ism_Seo_A_012: Oh...
MID_SE_Ism_Seo_A_013: Yet how can we have a temple without a god\nin residence?
MID_SE_Ism_Seo_A_014: <NCA>"Maybe you don't need one."
MID_SE_Ism_Seo_A_015: What? Promised One...are you suggesting we\nabandon our faith?
MID_SE_Ism_Seo_A_016: <NCA>"No more than you ever have."
MID_SE_Ism_Seo_A_017: Hm. True. We children of Damascar kept the faith\neven after Yu Phas's death.
MID_SE_Ism_Seo_A_018: Long after the abominable Dagda executed our\ngoddess and destroyed her temple.
MID_SE_Ism_Seo_A_019: In truth, many of the proposals I have reviewed\nassume that there will be no god present.
MID_SE_Ism_Seo_A_020: The people of Saramis will likely continue to offer\ntheir prayers in the absence of a deity.
MID_SE_Ism_Seo_A_021: My only fear is that after long months and years\npass, praying in an empty temple...
MID_SE_Ism_Seo_A_022: the people may eventually forget the great debt we\nowe to Yu Phas.
MID_SE_Ism_Seo_A_023: As the queen responsible for directing her people,\nis that an outcome I can allow?
MID_SE_Ism_Seo_A_024: <NCA>"It would be an age of humans."
MID_SE_Ism_Seo_A_025: And no longer an age of gods, hmm?
MID_SE_Ism_Seo_A_026: If such a world is to come, I suppose I am the natural\ncandidate to usher it in.
MID_SE_Ism_Seo_A_027: I have no bloodmark, after all. Monarchs with no\nconnection to a divine lineage are rare.
MID_SE_Ism_Seo_A_028: <NCA>"I expect much from you."
MID_SE_Ism_Seo_A_029: The idea is akin to turning our back on the gods. But\nif this is to be a world of humans, it must be done.
MID_SE_Ism_Seo_A_030: I will take up your unorthodox view. On my name,\nI vow to fulfill your expectations.
MID_SE_Ism_Seo_S: <EDH>
MID_SE_Ism_Seo_S_001: Promised One!
MID_SE_Ism_Seo_S_002: I am gladdened to see you return to us.
MID_SE_Ism_Seo_S_003: I had faith that you would escape, but the waiting\nleft me anxious.
MID_SE_Ism_Seo_S_004: <NCA>"I'm sorry I worried you."
MID_SE_Ism_Seo_S_005: <NCB>"I'm sorry you had to wait."
MID_SE_Ism_Seo_S_006: As you should be. If it was your aim to try my\nnerves, you hit the mark too well for my taste.
MID_SE_Ism_Seo_S_007: But let me choose instead to rejoice in your\ntriumphant return.
MID_SE_Ism_Seo_S_008: The other brave warriors in our company were\nworried as well. Have you seen to them yet?
MID_SE_Ism_Seo_S_009: <NCA>"Only you, Theodora."
MID_SE_Ism_Seo_S_010: <NCB>"I wanted you to be the first one I returned to."
MID_SE_Ism_Seo_S_011: <ACA>Hehe. Ah, so I am special to you. It was worth\nlooking my best today, in that case.
MID_SE_Ism_Seo_S_012: <ACB>Oh? If I command your attention, Promised One,\nthen it was worth looking my best today.
MID_SE_Ism_Seo_S_013: Don't nod to that as if I meant it seriously. It was\nobviously a jest.
MID_SE_Ism_Seo_S_014: I...had hoped to see you too. I waited patiently for\nyou to return, Promised One.
MID_SE_Ism_Seo_S_015: Even after warring with gods, there is no rest for me\nas queen.
MID_SE_Ism_Seo_S_016: Not when I have been given the task of ushering in\nthe age of humans you spoke of.
MID_SE_Ism_Seo_S_017: I had hoped you would be there beside me as I walk\nthat difficult path.
MID_SE_Ism_Seo_S_018: Though given this arm of mine, I cannot be certain\nI will walk it to its end.
MID_SE_Ism_Seo_S_019: Mm...
MID_SE_Ism_Seo_S_020: For whatever time I have left, can I count upon you\nto spend it with me?
MID_SE_Ism_Seo_S_021: <NCA>"I will stay beside you."
MID_SE_Ism_Seo_S_024: 
MID_SE_Ism_Seo_S_022: <RSDS>Ah...that puts me at ease. It has been so long since\nI felt this way.
MID_SE_Ism_Seo_S_023: When I bring about the age of humans, I hope you\nare there with me to see it firsthand.